From cb8961616b8d0ac7afea44627d93015ea0ebb4fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ivanmeler <i_ivan@windowslive.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:41:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: handle missing optional driver queries and memory
 binding

The loader exposes promoted instance queries even with older driver APIs.
Several physical-device query wrappers check the core entry point but
unconditionally call its KHR alias when the core pointer is absent. Both
can be missing on Vulkan 1.0 drivers, causing the same null-call failure
as the surface-format query.

Share core/KHR dispatch and fall back to the corresponding required 1.0
query for basic features, properties, formats, memory, queue families and
sparse-image formats. Preserve output headers, extension chains and array
capacity semantics. Reject image-format extension queries when neither
newer entry point can implement them. Regenerate the required driver-table
entries from the updated generator.

Use either available spelling of BindImageMemory2 for swapchain memory
binding. Allocate swapchain images eagerly if neither exists, and return
FEATURE_NOT_PRESENT for an unsupported explicit bind instead of calling
null. Preserve intercepted native-buffer binding data.

Check surface-format extension enumeration errors before allocating or
reading its output, and avoid a second enumeration with an empty vector.

Validation: extracted host regressions reproduce the previous null call
and allocation abort. The fixed code passes 208 dispatch/array/binding
cases and 7 enumeration fault cases under ASan/UBSan. Android build and
game runtime tests remain pending the user's build.

Change-Id: I7cf4bfaa0083c0e8fc64ddcd1f4fa11eff3adc72
---
